bal news halifax  up next the tiny island off the coast of  bc that played a mighty role in the  second world war  former u.s senator bob dole a giant in  the republican party has died dole was  one of the longest serving republicans  in the senate representing his home  state of kansas for 27 years he ran for  president three times and unsuccessfully  challenged bill clinton in the 1996  election dole a celebrated veteran  fought in the second world war in 1945  he was seriously injured on the  battlefield in italy and left for dead  he recovered but lost the use of his  right arm dole had been in declining  health and was diagnosed with stage four  lung cancer earlier this year according  to his family he passed away in his  sleep this morning he was 98.  this week will mark 80 years since japan  attacked pearl harbor changing the  course of the second world war what you  may not know is how that attack in  hawaii led to increased security  concerns along canada's west coast jay  durant looks into the forgotten history  of a small island off british columbia  that was fortified to protect the  pacific  december 7th  1941  a date which will live  in infamy this year marks the 80th  anniversary of japan's attack on pearl  harbor an event that put defenses along  north america's west coast on high alert  including here on tiny york island and  johnston straits a site the canadian  military had picked as a good location  for coastal defense before the outbreak  of the second world war that made the  war suddenly seem real  because  people on the west coast of canada  hadn't felt  the significance of the war suddenly it  the western side of the country felt  very vulnerable construction on this  coastal defense site began in 1937 and  during the war york island became home  for about 200 military personnel  docks were constructed guns mounted and  searchlights installed to help fortify  bc's coast they had an expert come in  coastal defense come from britain he  thought york island was a good location  because it's north of vancouver japanese  planes that might be  on route over the north end of vancouver  island heading towards vancouver could  be intercepted  so this is my dad here in the middle  schulte's father was stationed there  there were some long days isolated on  this remote island  told me about  them having a ball diamond so they  played baseball there other than that  i don't remember him talking about  other other activities these are stairs  leading up to the officer's quarters  nature has reclaimed a lot of the site  but some structures still remain a  reminder of a time filled with so much  tension when bc faced uncertainty about  potential attacks during the second  world war there was that sense that  it could happen  and so i think that there was fear  and you know there was some trepidation  that  they could be in danger and that they  might have a role to play  jay durant global news  and that is global national for this  sunday night i'm robin gill tonight your  canada is the sunset on georgian bay we  would love to see your corner of the  country so please keep sending your  photos to viewers at globalnational.com  thank you for watching donna friesen  will be back at the anchor desk tomorrow  and i'll see you next weekend  [Music]  you
 

